post.description:
From an enrolment-only session this also issues the full session the caller was waiting
for: the passkey they just added is exactly what the enrolment session existed to get,
so it is retired and replaced in the same call.

portOutcomes.description:
How each port came to be what it is: kept as requested, or moved and why. Only interesting
when IReadOnlyDictionary&lt;string, int&gt;? CreateShardRequest.PreferredPorts was supplied, which is the import case;
a fresh deployment preferred nothing, so every entry reads as "nothing discovered".

state.description:
What the activation file says on its own: Valid, Expired, or Invalid (unreadable/moved-machine activation);
    or Unconfirmed while its spire cannot identify its machine (typically a start that ran ahead of the network) and is
    checking again. An Unconfirmed licence stands as it did when that spire last confirmed it since it started, and stands Invalid when it has not

memorySwapMb.description:
Total memory + swap in MiB. Docker/Podman semantics:
-1 = unlimited swap; 0 = runtime default (typically 2x MemoryLimitMb);
&gt;0 must be &gt;= MemoryLimitMb. Not meaningful when MemoryLimitMb = 0.

